From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Lebedev <sergey@lebedev.mobi>
Date: Thu, 16 Jul 2026 00:27:32 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] mtd: nand: mtk: EN751221 -- disable the in-band
 bad-block-marker swap, main data and OOB

EN751221 tracks bad blocks with a BMT (an out-of-band back-reference
table managed by the bootloader), NOT the MediaTek in-band factory-BBM
scheme this driver implements by default -- and the bootbase `flash`
writer stores raw page data, main and spare, verbatim with no BBM
relocation of any kind. Two call sites apply that scheme and both are
wrong here, for the same reason:

 - mtk_nfc_bad_mark_swap() exchanges a live main-data byte with
   oob_poi[0] on every page read/write. For our geometry it clobbers
   main-data offset 2000 (0x7D0) of every page: one wrong byte per
   2048-byte page, which most block checksums still happen to survive
   but which corrupts xz decompression near the end of the rootfs --
   the observed "SQUASHFS error: xz decompression failed" boot failure.
 - oob_ptr() moves the bad-mark sector's FDM to the front of oob_poi,
   the OOB-side half of the same in-band convention. Leaving this
   active desyncs Linux's OOB byte offsets from the vendor bootloader
   and the on-flash BMT/BBT tables it writes: en75_bmt's FDM tag
   lookup at ooboffs 0 would silently land on physical sector 3's
   spare bytes instead of sector 0's, for our page geometry
   (bad_mark.sec == 3).

The vendor read/write path never does either swap; neither should we.
Select the no-op swap for the main-data path (mtk_nfc_bad_mark_swap
then has no callers, so tag it __maybe_unused to keep
-Werror=unused-function happy) and drop oob_ptr()'s swap outright.
This driver copy is EN751221-only in the econet build, so an
unconditional change is correct here.

Signed-off-by: Sergey Lebedev <sergey@lebedev.mobi>
---
--- a/drivers/mtd/nand/raw/mtk_nand.c
+++ b/drivers/mtd/nand/raw/mtk_nand.c
@@ -204,20 +204,22 @@ static inline u8 *data_ptr(struct nand_c
 static inline u8 *oob_ptr(struct nand_chip *chip, int i)
 {
 	struct mtk_nfc_nand_chip *mtk_nand = to_mtk_nand(chip);
-	u8 *poi;
 
-	/* map the sector's FDM data to free oob:
-	 * the beginning of the oob area stores the FDM data of bad mark sectors
+	/*
+	 * Mainline moves the bad-mark sector's FDM to the front of oob_poi,
+	 * mirroring the in-band factory-BBM byte swap disabled below in
+	 * mtk_nfc_set_bad_mark_ctl() for the same reason: EN751221 uses a
+	 * BMT for bad blocks, not that scheme, and the bootbase `flash`
+	 * writer stores raw page data -- data AND spare -- verbatim with no
+	 * relocation. Leaving this OOB-side swap active desyncs Linux's OOB
+	 * byte offsets from the vendor bootloader and the on-flash BMT/BBT
+	 * tables it writes: en75_bmt's FDM tag lookup at ooboffs 0 would
+	 * silently land on physical sector 3's spare bytes instead of
+	 * sector 0's, for our page geometry (bad_mark.sec == 3). This
+	 * driver copy is EN751221-only in the econet build, so an
+	 * unconditional change is correct here.
 	 */
-
-	if (i < mtk_nand->bad_mark.sec)
-		poi = chip->oob_poi + (i + 1) * mtk_nand->fdm.reg_size;
-	else if (i == mtk_nand->bad_mark.sec)
-		poi = chip->oob_poi;
-	else
-		poi = chip->oob_poi + i * mtk_nand->fdm.reg_size;
-
-	return poi;
+	return chip->oob_poi + i * mtk_nand->fdm.reg_size;
 }
 
 static inline int mtk_data_len(struct nand_chip *chip)
@@ -733,7 +735,7 @@ static void mtk_nfc_no_bad_mark_swap(str
 	/* nop */
 }
 
-static void mtk_nfc_bad_mark_swap(struct mtd_info *mtd, u8 *buf, int raw)
+static void __maybe_unused mtk_nfc_bad_mark_swap(struct mtd_info *mtd, u8 *buf, int raw)
 {
 	struct nand_chip *chip = mtd_to_nand(mtd);
 	struct mtk_nfc_nand_chip *nand = to_mtk_nand(chip);
@@ -1176,7 +1178,14 @@ static void mtk_nfc_set_bad_mark_ctl(str
 	if (mtd->writesize == 512) {
 		bm_ctl->bm_swap = mtk_nfc_no_bad_mark_swap;
 	} else {
-		bm_ctl->bm_swap = mtk_nfc_bad_mark_swap;
+		/*
+		 * EN751221 uses a BMT for bad blocks, not the MediaTek in-band
+		 * factory-BBM scheme, and the bootbase `flash` writer stores
+		 * raw page data with no BBM relocation. The in-band swap would
+		 * corrupt one live main-data byte per page (sector 3, offset
+		 * 464 -> page offset 0x7D0) and break squashfs/xz. Disable it.
+		 */
+		bm_ctl->bm_swap = mtk_nfc_no_bad_mark_swap;
 		bm_ctl->sec = mtd->writesize / mtk_data_len(nand);
 		bm_ctl->pos = mtd->writesize % mtk_data_len(nand);
 	}
